==Russian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|по́дданный}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-подданный.ogg}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{af|ru|подда́ть|-анный}}.

====Participle====
{{head|ru|past passive participle|head=по́дданный}}

# {{participle of|ru|подда́ть||past|pass|pfv}}

=====Declension=====
{{ru-decl-adj|по́дданный|a'(2)}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|ru|pl|poddany}}, which is a calque of {{der|ru|la|subditus}}, probably mediated via {{bor|ru|zle-ort|подданыи}}. {{surf|ru|подда́ть|-анный}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|по́дданный|+|f=по́дданная|a=an}}

# [[national]] (a person owing allegiance to a state)
# [[citizen]] (a person who possesses citizenship of a state)
# [[subject]] {{gloss|legal member of a state}}

=====Usage notes=====
Used with citizens of monarchies. For citizens of republics гражданин is used instead.

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-table|по́дданный|+|a=an}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|ru|граждани́н}}
